WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.646 --> 00:00:02.238
We got Dr. Isaacson.

2
00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.049
All right. You guys go check it out.
I'm expected at the office.

3
00:00:07.253 --> 00:00:08.242
Hubb?

4
00:00:08.454 --> 00:00:11.582
Get ready for the smackdown.
He's gonna come at you hard.

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

6
00:00:55.168 --> 00:00:57.830
- Who is it?
- N.Y.P.D.

7
00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.232
- Dr. Isaacson?
- Yeah.

8
00:01:02.441 --> 00:01:05.535
Detective Ornelas. N.Y.P.D.
This is my partner. Detective Ward.

9
00:01:05.745 --> 00:01:07.975
- We'd like to ask a couple questions.
- Why?

10
00:01:08.347 --> 00:01:09.905
What do you want?
Why are you here?

11
00:01:10.116 --> 00:01:13.745
Calm down. We just wanna ask you
a few questions about a patient.

12
00:01:13.953 --> 00:01:16.547
Patient? What patient?
Come on. you know what time it is?

13
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.388
Listen. I'm sorry. I must go.
I really didn't do anything.

14
00:01:20.593 --> 00:01:22.959
- I'm sorry. Good night.
- Doctor. if we could-

15
00:01:25.264 --> 00:01:28.859
Douche bag's pinned out of his mind.
He thinks we're here to bust him.

16
00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:33.167
Dr. Isaacson. please.

17
00:01:33.372 --> 00:01:36.637
We have reason to believe your life
is in danger. grave danger.

18
00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:40.577
We think one of your patients
is trying to kill you.

19
00:01:45.852 --> 00:01:46.841
Kill me?

20
00:01:47.053 --> 00:01:50.420
I'm Agent Salinger with Interpol.
We're assisting in this manhunt.

21
00:01:50.623 --> 00:01:54.024
Why would a patient wanna kill me?
I'm an orthopedist.

22
00:01:54.227 --> 00:01:57.526
This man's a psychotic. He's already
butchered seven doctors in Europe.

23
00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:00.563
We got some serious evidence
to suggest you may be next.

24
00:02:00.766 --> 00:02:02.063
Have you ever seen this man?

25
00:02:04.437 --> 00:02:07.201
No. no. I don't think so.

26
00:02:07.406 --> 00:02:10.967
Does the name Timothy Sherwood
mean anything to you. doctor?

27
00:02:11.177 --> 00:02:13.907
No. How do you know
he's a patient of mine?

28
00:02:14.113 --> 00:02:15.171
We have his footprint.

29
00:02:15.381 --> 00:02:17.906
Yeah. the shoe was manufactured
by AGM Biomechanics...

30
00:02:18.117 --> 00:02:22.451
...exclusively for the Isaacson Institute.
model K-A-F-O 1-2-1.

31
00:02:22.655 --> 00:02:24.418
K- A-F-O 1-2-1?

32
00:02:24.624 --> 00:02:26.717
We started prescribing
that three years ago.

33
00:02:27.093 --> 00:02:28.958
We've used it on hundreds
of our patients.

34
00:02:29.161 --> 00:02:32.221
Well. then we're gonna need
to review all of your files.

35
00:02:32.832 --> 00:02:33.924
Right now?

36
00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:38.160
Doctor. we need to find this man
before he finds you.

37
00:02:39.805 --> 00:02:43.434
- What are you trying to do here. Ella?
- I'm doing my job.

38
00:02:43.643 --> 00:02:46.237
You have any idea of the shitstorm
you've gotten me into?

39
00:02:46.445 --> 00:02:49.039
- We're just trying to get to the truth.
- I get it.

40
00:02:49.682 --> 00:02:53.550
You need to remember there's what
people wanna hear. wanna believe...

41
00:02:53.753 --> 00:02:56.187
...there's everything else.
then there's the truth.

42
00:02:56.389 --> 00:02:59.688
And since when is that okay?
I can't believe you're saying this to me.

43
00:02:59.892 --> 00:03:01.951
The truth means responsibility. Arnie.

44
00:03:02.161 --> 00:03:05.130
Exactly. which is why
everyone dreads it.

45
00:03:10.236 --> 00:03:11.863
Look...

46
00:03:15.841 --> 00:03:20.540
The IBBC is using one assassin
for all their hits...

47
00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:23.778
...and we've tracked him here
to New York.

48
00:03:25.418 --> 00:03:28.080
This guy can bury them.

49
00:03:31.123 --> 00:03:34.286
They want me to put a gun
to your head.

50
00:03:34.727 --> 00:03:37.491
You don't find this guy.
and I mean quick...

51
00:03:37.697 --> 00:03:39.927
...they're gonna make me
pull the trigger.

52
00:03:45.204 --> 00:03:47.138
- Do you want dessert?
- No. thank you.

53
00:03:47.673 --> 00:03:49.300
I'd like one.

54
00:03:49.642 --> 00:03:52.236
This is a game that rewards
patience and balance.

55
00:03:52.445 --> 00:03:55.937
You must think like a man of action
and act like a man of thought.

56
00:04:07.927 --> 00:04:09.155
Gentlemen.

57
00:04:09.362 --> 00:04:12.126
<i>Sorry to disturb you at home.
I'm afraid this couldn't wait.</i>

58
00:04:12.898 --> 00:04:14.126
Yes?

59
00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:16.528
<i>Salinger was in Milan.</i>

60
00:04:16.736 --> 00:04:18.260
<i>Whitman too.</i>

61
00:04:18.471 --> 00:04:19.733
<i>They have the scent.</i>

62
00:04:19.939 --> 00:04:23.807
<i>It's only a matter of time
before they find our consultant.</i>

63
00:04:30.883 --> 00:04:32.407
Any recommendations?

64
00:04:32.618 --> 00:04:34.643
<i>I strongly advise
against doing anything...</i>

65
00:04:34.854 --> 00:04:37.220
<i>...that would heighten your exposure
right now.</i>

66
00:04:37.423 --> 00:04:39.755
<i>Wilhelm. we've leveraged ourselves
over the edge.</i>

67
00:04:39.959 --> 00:04:42.894
<i>If we don't meet the delivery date.
buyers will cancel orders...</i>

68
00:04:43.095 --> 00:04:44.426
<i>...our plans will implode...</i>

69
00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.996
<i>...and this bank will be left
a bill it cannot pay.</i>

70
00:04:47.199 --> 00:04:49.429
<i>Heightening exposure
is the least of our problems.</i>

71
00:04:49.635 --> 00:04:51.899
<i>I agree.
We're about to engage Calvini's sons.</i>

72
00:04:52.104 --> 00:04:54.265
<i>We can't allow anyone
to put our agenda at risk.</i>

73
00:04:54.473 --> 00:04:56.771
<i>We must sever all ties
with the consultant.</i>

74
00:04:56.976 --> 00:04:59.137
<i>Consider the mark. gentlemen.</i>

75
00:04:59.345 --> 00:05:04.282
<i>Doing this could be
a very messy affair.</i>

76
00:05:04.483 --> 00:05:06.713
<i>Well. then make it one.</i>

77
00:05:06.919 --> 00:05:09.513
<i>I don't know why you pay me
to advise on these matters.</i>

78
00:05:09.722 --> 00:05:13.590
<i>It is clear that you don't want my
counsel. only my corroboration.</i>

79
00:05:13.793 --> 00:05:17.388
<i>Really. Wilhelm. We've had
just about all we can take of you.</i>

80
00:05:17.596 --> 00:05:22.556
<i>Yes. I've had about all I can take
of myself.</i>

81
00:05:23.502 --> 00:05:25.800
<i>How would you like us to proceed?</i>

82
00:05:30.576 --> 00:05:34.307
Cassian. what does one do when
there's no way out of a situation?

83
00:05:34.713 --> 00:05:36.578
If there's no way out...

84
00:05:37.783 --> 00:05:41.150
...the best thing is
to find a way further in.

85
00:06:01.073 --> 00:06:03.837
- Fucking disgusting. you know that?
- What are you. my mother?

86
00:06:04.043 --> 00:06:06.944
No. but I could be your old man
for all you know. asshole.

87
00:06:18.057 --> 00:06:19.615
Hey. doc.

88
00:06:22.027 --> 00:06:23.426
Gabriel Hansen?

89
00:06:24.163 --> 00:06:27.724
I don't know.
My associate handled this.

90
00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:31.364
Well. the address
is a post-office box...

91
00:06:32.238 --> 00:06:34.763
...and he paid cash
for all of his medical bills.

92
00:06:36.208 --> 00:06:39.837
There are no diagnostic photos.
Why?

93
00:06:41.847 --> 00:06:43.610
- I don't know.
- Is there a number?

94
00:06:43.816 --> 00:06:49.584
Yeah. 212-157-6421.

95
00:06:55.461 --> 00:06:56.450
It's a dead line.

96
00:07:02.635 --> 00:07:04.865
I'll put a call in to Hubby.
have her run it down.

97
00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.868
See if we can't get a crack warrant
for the P.O. Box in Jersey.

98
00:07:12.478 --> 00:07:15.970
What do all these GT's
next to the appointment entries mean?

99
00:07:16.615 --> 00:07:19.243
We have a kickback account
with Go Taxi...

100
00:07:19.752 --> 00:07:22.516
...and they indicate when we
use their service for a patient.

101
00:07:25.324 --> 00:07:27.019
<i>Hey. Hubb says you caught a lead.</i>

102
00:07:27.226 --> 00:07:29.160
Yeah. we've got an address.
We're en route.

103
00:07:29.361 --> 00:07:30.953
<i>- What is it?
- Well. it could be him.</i>

104
00:07:31.163 --> 00:07:32.391
<i>- Really?
- Yeah.</i>

105
00:07:32.598 --> 00:07:35.431
<i>Well. they gotta bring him in now.
This is our last shot.</i>

106
00:07:35.634 --> 00:07:37.192
What do you mean. "our last shot"?

107
00:07:37.403 --> 00:07:40.270
<i>Arnie and I had it out last night.
and our clock's run out.</i>

108
00:07:40.806 --> 00:07:44.537
<i>If we don't get this guy right now.
it's over.</i>

109
00:07:46.345 --> 00:07:48.609
Well. it better be him. then.

110
00:08:00.559 --> 00:08:02.891
I'm here. Yeah.

111
00:08:06.232 --> 00:08:07.221
I know that.

112
00:08:07.433 --> 00:08:09.230
This is definitely the right address?

113
00:08:09.435 --> 00:08:13.428
Checked the log myself. This is where
they dropped him off every time.

114
00:08:14.673 --> 00:08:16.664
Well. he could be anywhere.

115
00:08:19.612 --> 00:08:22.274
- What do you think he was doing?
- Beats the shit out of me.

116
00:08:22.481 --> 00:08:23.539
It's a big. empty lot.

117
00:08:23.749 --> 00:08:26.616
Well. I'm starving. I'm gonna
get something. You want anything?

118
00:08:26.819 --> 00:08:27.808
Yeah. a coffee. black.

119
00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.386
I'm going back down to
headquarters after this.

120
00:08:30.589 --> 00:08:32.420
Okay. all right.

121
00:08:40.065 --> 00:08:41.032
Right. bye.

122
00:08:41.233 --> 00:08:43.292
How long do you think
this has been like this?

123
00:08:43.502 --> 00:08:45.333
I don't know. but we need to find out.

124
00:08:45.537 --> 00:08:47.368
The doctor's records say
the last time...

125
00:08:47.573 --> 00:08:50.440
...somebody got dropped off here
was five weeks ago.

126
00:08:51.043 --> 00:08:53.910
I mean. there's not even
a temporary office or anything.

127
00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.571
- How you doing?
- How you doing?

128
00:09:13.399 --> 00:09:16.095
Son of a bitch.

129
00:09:21.573 --> 00:09:22.597
What's the matter?

130
00:09:22.808 --> 00:09:25.470
I just made our perp.
Eleven o'clock. blue overcoat.

131
00:09:28.147 --> 00:09:30.707
- You sure that's him?
- A hundred percent.

132
00:09:31.383 --> 00:09:33.214
- Where did he come from?
- Shit if I know.

133
00:09:33.419 --> 00:09:36.149
I'm at the counter and
I see him rolling past the window.

134
00:09:36.355 --> 00:09:37.720
- Wanna go for the collar?
- No.

135
00:09:37.923 --> 00:09:40.551
We tail him. find out where he sleeps.
then take him down.

136
00:09:40.759 --> 00:09:43.694
A. B. C. Keep the box tight.

137
00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:06.507
<i>- Five-oh-two-six. Designator?
- Samuel Koppler.</i>

138
00:11:08.313 --> 00:11:09.541
<i>Message:</i>

139
00:11:10.249 --> 00:11:13.116
<i>Your uncle
wishes to see you immediately.</i>

140
00:11:13.318 --> 00:11:14.717
<i>Response?</i>

141
00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:19.653
The Guggenheim. fifth floor
of the rotunda. 40 minutes.

142
00:12:05.304 --> 00:12:06.828
- Hi. how you doing?
- Hello.

143
00:12:07.039 --> 00:12:09.269
N.Y.P.D. I need to
speak to your security chief.

144
00:12:09.475 --> 00:12:10.874
Okay. one moment.

145
00:12:11.977 --> 00:12:13.535
Rick?

146
00:12:14.179 --> 00:12:17.512
How you doing? Detective Ornelas.
I need to be able to clear security.

147
00:12:17.716 --> 00:12:19.149
- Okay.
- Thanks.

148
00:12:24.356 --> 00:12:26.017
We're clear.

149
00:12:57.523 --> 00:12:59.855
Directly behind me.

150
00:13:07.666 --> 00:13:09.497
There you go. Thank you.

151
00:14:00.419 --> 00:14:02.546
Who's the old scag
sitting next to him?

152
00:14:02.754 --> 00:14:05.951
I don't know. but I saw him at the
bank's headquarters in Luxembourg.

153
00:14:06.592 --> 00:14:09.254
You don't look well today.

154
00:14:09.695 --> 00:14:12.163
We all begin better than we end.

155
00:14:12.965 --> 00:14:15.297
What would you prefer your ending
to be like?

156
00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:20.437
Oh. more purposeful.
and certainly more climactic.

157
00:14:20.939 --> 00:14:22.531
A finale.

158
00:14:23.175 --> 00:14:24.767
A finale.

159
00:14:24.977 --> 00:14:28.504
Circumstances can always
be arranged.

160
00:14:29.514 --> 00:14:31.379
As much as the thought
appeals to me...

161
00:14:31.583 --> 00:14:35.246
...I'm afraid your consideration
is needed elsewhere.

162
00:14:36.121 --> 00:14:38.646
- What is this?
- Salinger.

163
00:14:39.224 --> 00:14:42.057
The method and manner
is entirely up to you.

164
00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:47.459
Your principle would simply like him
to vanish without a trace.

165
00:14:49.735 --> 00:14:53.034
- Any other provisions?
- Yes.

166
00:14:53.238 --> 00:14:54.535
No mistakes.

167
00:14:57.876 --> 00:14:59.673
I'll follow.

168
00:15:04.883 --> 00:15:08.182
- Where's Iggy going?
- Following a new lead.

169
00:15:36.982 --> 00:15:38.347
Shit.

170
00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:39.915
We gotta go.

171
00:15:41.553 --> 00:15:44.647
N.Y.P.D. Lock your hands
behind your head.

172
00:15:48.694 --> 00:15:49.820
Do it now.

173
00:15:50.429 --> 00:15:52.158
They'll never let you bring me in.

174
00:15:52.364 --> 00:15:54.423
Do it. or I'll take you down.

175
00:15:57.636 --> 00:15:58.898
- Cuffs.
- On the belt.

176
00:16:09.414 --> 00:16:10.779
There's a guy right up there.

177
00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:40.603
- Where'd he-?
- Up there! Up there!

178
00:16:51.289 --> 00:16:52.278
Get down!

179
00:16:59.097 --> 00:17:00.962
- God! Oh. my God!
- It's okay.

180
00:17:03.735 --> 00:17:04.724
Down there.

181
00:17:14.579 --> 00:17:16.410
Shit.

182
00:17:36.668 --> 00:17:37.657
Drop the gun.

183
00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:42.701
- If I drop the gun. we'll both die.
- I said. drop the gun!

184
00:17:42.908 --> 00:17:46.867
They're here for me but they'll kill
you too. Now help me get this off.

185
00:17:48.413 --> 00:17:49.607
I can't breathe.

186
00:18:12.571 --> 00:18:14.300
Stairs.

187
00:18:26.351 --> 00:18:28.251
- Fuck.
- You okay?

188
00:18:31.389 --> 00:18:32.856
The ramp is the only way out.

189
00:20:48.126 --> 00:20:49.753
Hey.

190
00:20:51.429 --> 00:20:53.989
Don't you fucking dare.

191
00:21:47.052 --> 00:21:49.247
<i>I'm calling from the dark side.</i>

192
00:21:49.454 --> 00:21:53.117
<i>- Sorry. Sorry. Sorry.
- I'm calling from the-</i>

193
00:22:30.962 --> 00:22:32.259
Get back.

194
00:22:52.684 --> 00:22:54.345
I told you.

195
00:22:56.387 --> 00:22:58.753
What? You told me what?

196
00:23:00.291 --> 00:23:03.192
They'd never let you bring me in.

197
00:23:29.354 --> 00:23:30.343
Fuck. fuck.

198
00:23:40.465 --> 00:23:42.729
<i>Move away from the building.</i>

199
00:23:42.934 --> 00:23:46.802
<i>Can everybody please
move away from the building?</i>

200
00:24:05.390 --> 00:24:07.358
They know you're coming.
We gotta hurry.

201
00:24:07.559 --> 00:24:10.892
- Where'd they find him?
- Sitting on a bench near the reservoir.

202
00:24:11.529 --> 00:24:14.657
- Has he said anything yet?
- Nothing. He's pretty shaken up.

203
00:24:14.866 --> 00:24:18.666
- Who else knows he's here?
- Everyone. Nothing I could do.

204
00:24:18.870 --> 00:24:21.270
Heavies from the Bureau
and Justice are on their way...

205
00:24:21.472 --> 00:24:23.167
<i>...with an unidentified third man.</i>

206
00:24:23.374 --> 00:24:26.104
- How long do I have?
- Five. 10 minutes. max.

207
00:24:26.311 --> 00:24:28.836
<i>- wanted for questioning
in an ongoing investigation.</i>

208
00:24:29.147 --> 00:24:34.449
<i>Now. a Guggenheim employee tells me
that while they were in the museum-</i>

209
00:25:10.655 --> 00:25:12.850
This isn't over.

210
00:25:30.942 --> 00:25:32.569
Are you sure about this?

211
00:25:38.483 --> 00:25:39.472
Just read it.

212
00:25:54.932 --> 00:25:56.923
- They recognize you?
- Don't think so.

213
00:26:01.406 --> 00:26:03.374
Back it up!

214
00:26:44.882 --> 00:26:47.009
<i>- ...screens came crashing down.
- How you doing?</i>

215
00:26:47.218 --> 00:26:50.551
<i>- There was glass everywhere.
- As compared to what?</i>

216
00:26:50.755 --> 00:26:52.586
<i>And just on the ground.</i>

217
00:26:52.790 --> 00:26:55.520
<i>When you heard all of this
commotion. did you think-?</i>

218
00:26:55.760 --> 00:26:57.694
Anything you need. Ellie.
just let me know.

219
00:26:57.895 --> 00:26:59.920
<i>- Thanks.
- I just heard gunshots.</i>

220
00:27:00.131 --> 00:27:02.258
<i>And people were hit
and screaming...</i>

221
00:27:02.467 --> 00:27:04.697
<i>...and people just started running
out the door...</i>

222
00:27:04.902 --> 00:27:06.631
<i>...and I didn't know
what was going on.</i>

223
00:27:06.838 --> 00:27:07.827
You okay?

224
00:27:08.606 --> 00:27:10.130
Yeah.

225
00:27:12.009 --> 00:27:14.102
You flip this guy.

226
00:27:14.579 --> 00:27:17.514
You make sure my partner
wasn't killed for nothing.

227
00:27:17.715 --> 00:27:21.446
<i>I know that- I think random people
were going down and-</i>

228
00:27:21.652 --> 00:27:26.180
<i>I mean. there was police running up
as other people were going down.</i>

229
00:27:38.703 --> 00:27:40.227
You ready for this?

230
00:28:16.908 --> 00:28:19.399
Good evening. Colonel Wexler.

231
00:28:21.212 --> 00:28:23.840
I'm Agent Louis Salinger.

232
00:28:24.649 --> 00:28:26.810
I know who you are.

233
00:28:28.686 --> 00:28:30.779
Of course you do.

234
00:28:32.824 --> 00:28:35.156
I was at the Guggenheim
this afternoon.

235
00:28:37.395 --> 00:28:38.987
<i>The assassin you met with...</i>

236
00:28:40.665 --> 00:28:42.758
<i>...I know you were his handler.</i>

237
00:28:42.967 --> 00:28:46.130
I know you arranged for him
to be killed at the behest of the bank...

238
00:28:46.337 --> 00:28:48.532
...because I was obviously
getting too close.

239
00:28:51.843 --> 00:28:54.539
But if a hit team at the Guggenheim
is what happens...

240
00:28:54.745 --> 00:28:57.543
...because I was
getting too close to him...

241
00:29:00.117 --> 00:29:03.814
...what do you think the bank'll do
when it realizes how close I am to you?

242
00:29:04.021 --> 00:29:08.583
Death comes for us all.
Agent Salinger.

243
00:29:09.327 --> 00:29:11.386
But based on everything
I've read about you...

244
00:29:11.596 --> 00:29:13.291
...you seem like the kind of man...

245
00:29:13.498 --> 00:29:16.399
...who aspired to die
for something more than this.

246
00:29:18.202 --> 00:29:22.696
Well. this is the difference
between truth and fiction.

247
00:29:24.041 --> 00:29:26.305
Fiction has to make sense.

248
00:29:29.080 --> 00:29:30.980
I'm confused. colonel.

249
00:29:34.151 --> 00:29:36.346
Why would a tried
and true communist...

250
00:29:37.455 --> 00:29:39.821
...a hardliner that spent 30 years
in the Stasi...

251
00:29:40.024 --> 00:29:42.185
...fighting against the evils
of capitalism...

252
00:29:42.894 --> 00:29:46.057
Why would this man waste his
final days working for an institution...

253
00:29:46.264 --> 00:29:49.427
...that was the very embodiment
of everything he once despised?

254
00:29:52.470 --> 00:29:55.337
You dedicated your life
to the communist ideal.

255
00:29:57.775 --> 00:30:01.142
You sacrificed everything
for the good of the party.

256
00:30:02.680 --> 00:30:04.011
For what?

257
00:30:07.752 --> 00:30:10.380
You lost your wife to betrayal...

258
00:30:11.022 --> 00:30:13.513
...your daughter to suicide...

259
00:30:14.892 --> 00:30:18.123
...and when the Wall fell.
your whole life fell apart with it.

260
00:30:18.429 --> 00:30:20.693
You know nothing about me.

261
00:30:21.265 --> 00:30:24.132
I was lost long before the Wall fell.

262
00:30:25.369 --> 00:30:30.068
I was once destined to become
a man much like yourself.

263
00:30:30.508 --> 00:30:32.305
True-hearted...

264
00:30:32.643 --> 00:30:34.611
...determined...

265
00:30:34.812 --> 00:30:36.780
...full of purpose.

266
00:30:37.782 --> 00:30:39.682
But...

267
00:30:40.151 --> 00:30:42.881
...character is easier kept
than recovered.

268
00:30:44.121 --> 00:30:47.989
We cannot control
the things life does to us.

269
00:30:48.659 --> 00:30:52.595
They are done before you know it.
and once they are done...

270
00:30:53.998 --> 00:30:56.159
...they make you do other things...

271
00:30:56.767 --> 00:30:59.964
...until at last.
everything comes between you...

272
00:31:01.005 --> 00:31:03.496
...and the man you wanted to be.

273
00:31:05.443 --> 00:31:06.910
No.

274
00:31:08.846 --> 00:31:12.009
We all have choices in life.
You made yours.

275
00:31:19.423 --> 00:31:21.220
Sometimes a man
can meet his destiny...

276
00:31:21.425 --> 00:31:23.256
...on the road he took to avoid it.

277
00:31:26.497 --> 00:31:29.227
Skarssen and that bank need to
answer for what they've done.

278
00:31:29.433 --> 00:31:31.401
They have to be brought to justice.

279
00:31:31.602 --> 00:31:33.536
You can help me do that.

280
00:31:33.871 --> 00:31:35.668
Justice...

281
00:31:36.507 --> 00:31:38.441
...is not possible.

282
00:31:39.110 --> 00:31:40.577
Why not?

283
00:31:41.045 --> 00:31:43.536
Because. Agent Salinger...

284
00:31:43.748 --> 00:31:47.684
...your idea of justice is an illusion.

285
00:31:48.452 --> 00:31:50.977
<i>Understand the very system
that you serve and protect...</i>

286
00:31:51.188 --> 00:31:54.715
<i>...will never allow anything to happen
to Skarssen or the bank.</i>

287
00:31:55.326 --> 00:31:56.884
On the contrary.

288
00:31:57.294 --> 00:32:01.355
The system guarantees
the IBBC's safety...

289
00:32:01.799 --> 00:32:05.030
...because everyone is involved.

290
00:32:05.836 --> 00:32:07.770
What do you mean. "everyone"?

291
00:32:10.608 --> 00:32:12.041
Hezbollah.

292
00:32:12.576 --> 00:32:14.510
CIA.

293
00:32:15.012 --> 00:32:16.707
The Columbian drug cartels.

294
00:32:17.114 --> 00:32:19.275
Russian organized crime.

295
00:32:19.483 --> 00:32:22.919
Governments of Iran. Germany.
China. your government.

296
00:32:23.154 --> 00:32:26.214
Every multinational corporation.
every one.

297
00:32:26.657 --> 00:32:30.957
They all need banks like the IBBC...

298
00:32:31.162 --> 00:32:36.031
...so that they can operate
within the black and gray latitudes.

299
00:32:36.434 --> 00:32:38.459
And this is why
your investigative efforts...

300
00:32:38.669 --> 00:32:42.230
...have either been ignored
or undermined...

301
00:32:42.440 --> 00:32:45.568
...and why you and I
will be quietly disposed of...

302
00:32:46.577 --> 00:32:51.605
...before any case against the bank
ever reaches a court of law.

303
00:32:57.755 --> 00:32:59.780
<i>So. what are we all
supposed to do?</i>

304
00:33:03.127 --> 00:33:05.391
We just supposed to give up...

305
00:33:05.696 --> 00:33:08.460
...and accept that
this is the way of the world?

306
00:33:12.937 --> 00:33:14.700
I'm not gonna do that.

307
00:33:16.140 --> 00:33:19.303
I still believe- I know...

308
00:33:19.510 --> 00:33:22.911
...that there has to be a way
to bring down this bank...

309
00:33:23.547 --> 00:33:25.913
...and you are gonna help me.

310
00:33:33.057 --> 00:33:35.218
You understand...

311
00:33:36.594 --> 00:33:40.325
...if you really want to
stop the IBBC...

312
00:33:41.065 --> 00:33:46.230
...you won't be able to do it within the
boundaries of your system of justice.

313
00:33:46.871 --> 00:33:49.237
You will have to go outside.

314
00:33:50.007 --> 00:33:51.565
Once you do...

315
00:33:53.244 --> 00:33:56.736
...there will always be
collateral damage.

316
00:34:01.485 --> 00:34:03.214
<i>Yes.</i>

317
00:34:04.288 --> 00:34:08.691
<i>Should you sacrifice your own ideals
for the greater good?</i>

318
00:34:09.860 --> 00:34:13.660
That's a difficult choice.
one I understand all too well...

319
00:34:14.598 --> 00:34:16.828
...but as you so eloquently put it...

320
00:34:17.268 --> 00:34:20.601
...sometimes a man
can meet his destiny...

321
00:34:20.805 --> 00:34:24.206
...on the road he took to avoid it.

322
00:34:36.120 --> 00:34:37.212
What?

323
00:34:37.421 --> 00:34:38.649
What are you doing?

324
00:34:39.290 --> 00:34:41.190
I think it's time for you to leave.

325
00:34:41.859 --> 00:34:46.558
- Leave? What are you talking about?
- You know what I'm talking about.

326
00:34:50.100 --> 00:34:51.931
No way. Lou.

327
00:34:52.136 --> 00:34:55.003
No fucking way.
You've already got him turned.

328
00:34:55.206 --> 00:34:58.607
Now go back in there
and get him to come in on his own.

329
00:34:59.143 --> 00:35:02.169
We can use everything.
We'll blow this whole thing wide open.

330
00:35:02.379 --> 00:35:04.677
- I don't think so.
- Why not?

331
00:35:04.882 --> 00:35:06.873
I'm not gonna make
the same mistake twice.

332
00:35:07.084 --> 00:35:10.645
- I can protect him. Lou.
- No. you can't. They'll get to him.

333
00:35:10.855 --> 00:35:12.413
If they can't. they'll get to you.

334
00:35:12.623 --> 00:35:15.023
If they can't get to you.
they'll get to your family.

335
00:35:27.738 --> 00:35:29.899
I can't just walk away from this.

336
00:35:31.208 --> 00:35:34.006
You're walking away
so I don't have to.

337
00:35:42.953 --> 00:35:44.386
How can you trust him?

338
00:35:44.855 --> 00:35:47.983
That relic in there
is looking for redemption.

339
00:35:48.192 --> 00:35:50.217
I'm the only one
who can give it to him.

340
00:35:51.295 --> 00:35:54.128
Then who gives it to you
when this is all over?

341
00:35:55.833 --> 00:35:57.892
You need to cut me loose.

342
00:36:00.504 --> 00:36:03.234
Tell them I escaped from custody.
whatever you have to.

343
00:36:03.440 --> 00:36:05.431
Just use my history.
They'll believe you.

344
00:36:05.643 --> 00:36:07.907
- I don't know.
- Ella. listen to me.

345
00:36:09.780 --> 00:36:11.145
Sometimes the hardest thing...

346
00:36:11.348 --> 00:36:14.340
...is to know which bridge to cross
and which to burn.

347
00:36:18.756 --> 00:36:20.951
I'm the one you burn.

348
00:37:20.551 --> 00:37:22.610
We've been waiting here
for an hour.

349
00:37:22.820 --> 00:37:26.620
I'm sorry. Martin. but none of us
have been able to reach them.

350
00:37:27.191 --> 00:37:31.685
Unfortunately. Mario and Enzo Calvini
are not known for their punctuality.

351
00:37:31.895 --> 00:37:33.726
They do realize this is the closing?

352
00:37:56.520 --> 00:37:57.851
Mr. White...

353
00:37:58.055 --> 00:38:01.513
...I've been instructed to escort you
and your associates from the building.

354
00:38:01.725 --> 00:38:03.784
Please gather your materials
and come with me.

355
00:38:03.994 --> 00:38:07.521
- Instructed by whom?
- Please. if you could just comply.

356
00:38:29.753 --> 00:38:32.381
Our father
never trusted these people.

357
00:38:34.024 --> 00:38:37.152
Thank you for telling us the truth.

358
00:38:40.764 --> 00:38:42.595
Had you not come forward...

359
00:38:42.800 --> 00:38:45.200
...we would have made
a terrible mistake today.

360
00:38:45.402 --> 00:38:48.064
I'm just glad I could be of service.

361
00:38:54.411 --> 00:38:58.074
I don't know. Jonas. I was told nothing.
I was simply thrown out.

362
00:38:58.549 --> 00:39:00.312
<i>They know.</i>

363
00:39:06.790 --> 00:39:11.090
Look. I can't discuss this right now.
I'll call you when I'm in the air.

364
00:39:36.687 --> 00:39:39.178
<i>Welcome to World News.
I'm Tristana Moore.</i>

365
00:39:39.389 --> 00:39:42.790
<i>We're live today in the
Democratic Republic of Niberia.</i>

366
00:39:42.993 --> 00:39:46.019
<i>As we go on air. we're getting reports
that thousands of troops...</i>

367
00:39:46.230 --> 00:39:49.859
<i>...loyal to General Charles Motomba's
Revolutionary Freedom Front...</i>

368
00:39:50.067 --> 00:39:52.627
<i>...are moving towards
the capital of Dénué.</i>

369
00:39:52.836 --> 00:39:55.771
<i>According to eyewitnesses.
several explosions have been heard...</i>

370
00:39:55.973 --> 00:39:59.966
<i>...and there've been heavy outbreaks
of gunfire in many parts of the city.</i>

371
00:40:00.177 --> 00:40:02.839
<i>The people of Niberia
have suffered greatly.</i>

372
00:40:03.046 --> 00:40:06.482
<i>It is time to begin a new chapter
in our country's history.</i>

373
00:40:06.683 --> 00:40:09.550
<i>We will not stop
until national liberation...</i>

374
00:40:09.753 --> 00:40:12.221
<i>...and the restoration of nationhood-</i>

375
00:40:17.027 --> 00:40:18.051
News about Martin?

376
00:40:19.029 --> 00:40:21.520
He didn't show up at his hotel
or at the airport.

377
00:40:21.732 --> 00:40:26.294
The Italian police have been unable
to locate his car or driver.

378
00:40:26.503 --> 00:40:30.166
I think Enzo and Mario Calvini
are sending us a message.

379
00:40:30.374 --> 00:40:32.740
How could they possibly
have found out?

380
00:40:36.513 --> 00:40:39.038
This is precisely
what we pay you to know.

381
00:40:39.249 --> 00:40:40.739
We're out of time and options.

382
00:40:41.151 --> 00:40:45.053
- We must make the deal with Sunay.
- How can we trust this man?

383
00:40:45.255 --> 00:40:48.383
The Israeli government
is his biggest customer.

384
00:40:48.592 --> 00:40:49.684
Why would he agree...

385
00:40:49.893 --> 00:40:53.454
...to help us provide missiles
to the Iranians and the Syrians...

386
00:40:53.664 --> 00:40:56.394
...that have a first-strike capability
against the Israelis?

387
00:40:56.600 --> 00:40:59.068
I know Sunay.
I believe he has every intention...

388
00:40:59.269 --> 00:41:01.100
...of selling you
the guidance systems...

389
00:41:01.538 --> 00:41:03.699
...because he's already provided
the Israelis...

390
00:41:03.907 --> 00:41:06.740
...with the countermeasures
to defeat them.

391
00:41:08.645 --> 00:41:11.443
Would the Turk really play
such a dangerous game?

392
00:41:12.950 --> 00:41:14.577
We are.

393
00:41:15.719 --> 00:41:17.983
The only way we can make this work...

394
00:41:18.188 --> 00:41:19.177
...is to guarantee...

395
00:41:19.389 --> 00:41:22.119
...that Sunay keeps this information
in complete confidence.

396
00:41:22.326 --> 00:41:26.262
If our buyers find out the missiles are
worthless. they'll pull all their orders...

397
00:41:26.463 --> 00:41:28.795
...and this bank will be left insolvent.

398
00:41:29.299 --> 00:41:31.233
Have him here
by tomorrow afternoon.

399
00:41:31.435 --> 00:41:34.666
Tomorrow he's going to
a funeral service for his cousin.

400
00:41:34.871 --> 00:41:36.736
He'll be unavailable till Monday.

401
00:41:37.374 --> 00:41:40.468
Unless of course.
you'd be willing to attend.

402
00:41:41.945 --> 00:41:43.742
Make the call.

403
00:41:46.216 --> 00:41:48.514
Get me Ahmet Sunay.

404
00:41:55.325 --> 00:41:57.293
It's tomorrow.

405
00:42:38.502 --> 00:42:41.062
It's right there.
Do you want to be escorted?

406
00:42:41.271 --> 00:42:42.704
We'll be fine. thank you.

407
00:42:48.679 --> 00:42:50.112
The Sunay funeral. please.

408
00:42:50.314 --> 00:42:52.612
It will be over soon.
You may wait here.

409
00:42:52.816 --> 00:42:56.809
- Is there a bathroom I could use?
- Just over there.

410
00:42:57.020 --> 00:42:59.955
- I won't be a moment.
- Right.

411
00:43:06.463 --> 00:43:08.624
- The signal?
- Good.

412
00:43:08.832 --> 00:43:10.197
<i>The Sunay funeral. please.</i>

413
00:43:10.834 --> 00:43:14.361
- Where'd you put the spike?
- Inside the lapel of his jacket.

414
00:43:15.572 --> 00:43:16.630
The lawyer?

415
00:43:17.841 --> 00:43:19.399
White?

416
00:43:19.643 --> 00:43:20.667
He's gone.

417
00:43:22.412 --> 00:43:26.280
I told you. there will always
be collateral damage...

418
00:43:26.483 --> 00:43:28.747
...when you take matters
into your own hands.

419
00:43:31.188 --> 00:43:32.212
Your plan is working.

420
00:43:33.156 --> 00:43:35.386
It has left Skarssen
with only one option.

421
00:43:35.592 --> 00:43:39.289
Record the conversation
and you'll gain your end.

422
00:43:41.465 --> 00:43:44.992
Sure they'll talk about Sunay's deal
with Israel and the countermeasures?

423
00:43:45.202 --> 00:43:46.533
It is the key issue.

424
00:43:46.737 --> 00:43:48.671
Once you let the Iranians
and Syrians...

425
00:43:48.872 --> 00:43:53.434
...hear that the missiles are completely
useless against the Israelis...

426
00:43:53.944 --> 00:43:59.780
...they will cancel their orders
and the IBBC will collapse.

427
00:44:08.458 --> 00:44:10.551
- Wilhelm.
- Ahmet.

428
00:44:11.061 --> 00:44:12.358
It's been a long time.

429
00:44:12.729 --> 00:44:13.718
<i>Yes.</i>

430
00:44:13.930 --> 00:44:15.795
<i>My sympathies for the loss
of your cousin.</i>

431
00:44:15.999 --> 00:44:17.227
Thank you.

432
00:44:17.434 --> 00:44:20.028
Jonas Skarssen. Ahmet Sunay.

433
00:44:20.237 --> 00:44:24.401
If you'd simply come to me in the
beginning. it would have been better.

434
00:44:27.244 --> 00:44:29.041
<i>Midday prayers will begin soon.</i>

435
00:44:29.246 --> 00:44:31.771
Should take a short time
to settle on the broad strokes.

436
00:44:31.982 --> 00:44:33.847
<i>The rest can be sorted out
at your leisure.</i>

437
00:44:34.050 --> 00:44:35.039
<i>We have 10 minutes.</i>

438
00:44:47.164 --> 00:44:50.497
Wilhelm. would you mind
if I spoke to Mr. Sunay alone?

439
00:44:55.739 --> 00:44:59.368
I believe I understand
the particulars of your situation.

440
00:44:59.576 --> 00:45:02.409
<i>Perhaps we should discuss this
in a more private place.</i>

441
00:45:02.612 --> 00:45:04.273
<i>Yes. of course.</i>

442
00:45:04.681 --> 00:45:07.309
<i>Allow me to show you something
very special.</i>

443
00:45:07.517 --> 00:45:11.283
<i>Something that very few outsiders
know exists.</i>

444
00:45:12.789 --> 00:45:17.488
<i>It's my understanding that the product
you purchased are the XW-41 s.</i>

445
00:45:17.961 --> 00:45:18.985
After you.

446
00:45:19.196 --> 00:45:21.528
<i>Yes. Forty-two hundred units.</i>

447
00:45:23.800 --> 00:45:26.633
What kind of guidance
are they currently equipped-?

448
00:45:31.875 --> 00:45:34.867
<i>They all need to be upgraded
with VOLCON systems.</i>

449
00:45:35.679 --> 00:45:37.340
<i>Launch platforms?</i>

450
00:45:37.547 --> 00:45:40.107
<i>Ground-based vehicles
and fixed-wing aircraft.</i>

451
00:45:50.560 --> 00:45:53.120
So you understand
I have a terminal deadline.

452
00:45:53.330 --> 00:45:55.127
First of February. yes.

453
00:45:55.332 --> 00:45:57.232
<i>- Can you meet it?
- To be sure.</i>

454
00:45:57.434 --> 00:46:01.029
<i>But you must arrange for the
end-user certificates. transport...</i>

455
00:46:01.238 --> 00:46:02.762
<i>We'll arrange for it all.</i>

456
00:46:02.973 --> 00:46:04.406
<i>Where would the work be done?</i>

457
00:46:04.608 --> 00:46:07.475
<i>Cyprus. I've a facility there.</i>

458
00:46:08.912 --> 00:46:12.473
<i>We would start retrofitting the worms
within a day of their arrival.</i>

459
00:46:12.682 --> 00:46:15.742
<i>So if you deliver them to me
within the next two weeks...</i>

460
00:46:15.952 --> 00:46:17.886
<i>...we'll meet your deadline.</i>

461
00:46:30.467 --> 00:46:33.732
I'm concerned that we limit any and all
knowledge of your involvement.

462
00:46:34.437 --> 00:46:37.838
<i>If we structure my involvement
through a thick veil of shells...</i>

463
00:46:39.042 --> 00:46:41.010
<i>...I don't foresee any complications.</i>

464
00:46:42.445 --> 00:46:45.175
- Sorry?
- You. Come here now.

465
00:46:45.382 --> 00:46:48.408
<i>Usually we would involve
our import partners from Russia.</i>

466
00:46:48.852 --> 00:46:50.285
What? I'm just a tourist.

467
00:46:50.487 --> 00:46:53.081
- Now. you must leave.
- Could you get that light out of-?

468
00:46:53.290 --> 00:46:55.918
Get your fucking-

469
00:46:58.094 --> 00:47:01.586
So. shall we discuss numbers?

470
00:47:02.032 --> 00:47:03.727
There is a more salient deal point...

471
00:47:03.934 --> 00:47:06.732
...that needs to be resolved
before we can do that.

472
00:47:06.937 --> 00:47:08.734
<i>And what point is that?</i>

473
00:47:09.739 --> 00:47:11.969
<i>The point of fidelity.</i>

474
00:47:19.149 --> 00:47:21.174
I know you provided
the Israeli government...

475
00:47:21.384 --> 00:47:24.319
...with the countermeasures
to this guidance system.

476
00:47:32.429 --> 00:47:34.488
Last year alone...

477
00:47:34.698 --> 00:47:38.259
...I did more than 300 million
in business with the Israelis.

478
00:47:41.972 --> 00:47:44.270
I would never put that at risk.

479
00:47:44.474 --> 00:47:48.672
How can I trust you not to divulge
this information to anyone else?

480
00:47:49.646 --> 00:47:52.171
It's mutual interest. not trust...

481
00:47:52.616 --> 00:47:55.244
...that will be the bond
of our relationship.

482
00:47:59.022 --> 00:48:01.855
Your compensation will be held
in an escrow account.

483
00:48:03.093 --> 00:48:05.288
<i>...released until our clients pay
in full.</i>

484
00:48:05.996 --> 00:48:07.327
And those are the terms.

485
00:48:10.100 --> 00:48:11.727
<i>The payout structure-</i>

486
00:48:14.137 --> 00:48:16.435
<i>The transfers will be begun
by tomorrow morning.</i>

487
00:48:16.640 --> 00:48:20.132
<i>Ehames will contact you with
the number for the escrow account.</i>

488
00:48:25.448 --> 00:48:28.440
So ends the bloody business
of the day.

489
00:48:41.297 --> 00:48:43.663
We're closed. I need you and Ehames
here tomorrow...

490
00:48:43.867 --> 00:48:46.427
...to work out all the details
with Sunay's people.

491
00:48:46.836 --> 00:48:49.566
Yes. We're on our way home.

492
00:48:57.414 --> 00:48:58.403
Wilhelm?

493
00:49:01.418 --> 00:49:02.817
Wake up.

494
00:52:03.867 --> 00:52:04.856
Who are you?

495
00:52:07.103 --> 00:52:08.866
I'm Louis Salinger.

496
00:52:18.848 --> 00:52:21.544
You don't have the authority
to arrest me.

497
00:52:23.820 --> 00:52:26.516
Who said anything
about arresting you?

498
00:52:30.860 --> 00:52:34.591
- What do you want?
- I want some fucking justice.

499
00:52:34.797 --> 00:52:38.494
Wait. wait. Wait.
Executing me won't change anything.

500
00:52:38.701 --> 00:52:41.192
There will be 100 other bankers
to take my place.

501
00:52:41.404 --> 00:52:44.396
Everything will continue.

502
00:52:44.607 --> 00:52:50.546
The only thing you'll succeed in doing
is to satisfy your own blood lust.

503
00:52:55.485 --> 00:52:56.918
And you know it.

504
00:53:51.574 --> 00:53:54.202
With compliments of Enzo
and Mario Calvini.

505
00:54:09.359 --> 00:54:10.826
Thank you.

506
00:54:11.305 --> 00:55:11.706
